; The repo pins Node 22 in .nvmrc and requires it via "engines" in
; package.json. Without this flag npm only prints a warning and installs
; anyway — which is how a Node 20 shell ends up with a dependency tree it
; cannot run. jsdom 30 pulls undici 8, which needs a Node 22 internal
; (webidl.util.markAsUncloneable); on Node 20 every vitest worker dies at
; startup and the suite reports "no tests" rather than a version error.
;
; Fail at install time instead.
engine-strict=true
